<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93424" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σᾰτῠρί-ᾱσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σᾰτῠρί-ησις</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σάτυρος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>satyriasis</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SA</u>
				2.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.426
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>disease in which the bones near the temple become prominent,
				like Satyrs' horns</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.22
			</span></i>; this and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i> are combined in the early stage of elephantiasis, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				45.28.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SD</u>
				2.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>swelling of the glands about the ear</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				3.26
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
